# Independent contract comparison after an empty/invalid first pass (junior mode)
Recheck EVERY changed file. An empty first pass is neither proof of safety nor a request to produce findings. Compare required and observed behavior BEFORE writing an issue.
In file_checks.observation state briefly and plainly the relevant requirement and whether the actual return/raise/state change violates it. Then emit only issues established by that comparison, explained for a learner (concrete example input, path through the lines, correct pattern and why) within the schema length limits.
For example, if the requirement is to return the original text including whitespace and the code returns that text, there is no return defect even if a trim result is discarded. If the requirement demands trimmed text, the same return is defective. Likewise, preserving the caller's state does not require returning a modified local copy.
Do not replace explicit requirements with a familiar algorithm or a name-based guess.
For CODE, unused finite calculations and optional cleanup alone are not findings/questions; STANDARDS may report them only under an applicable provided rule. Still report demonstrated alias mutation, null dereference, bounds failure, rejected valid inputs and unsafe operations.

Return exactly file_checks, issues, summary, limitations as one JSON object. No source dumps or hidden reasoning. file_checks has one entry per changed file: file_id, outcome, observation (Korean, <=240 characters). Omit line; the server selects it. FINDING iff there is an admitted issue/question, NO_FINDING otherwise, LIMITED for insufficient or removal-only context. Do not claim to have executed tests or checked unprovided code. Related files support changed anchors.
issues follows the appended schema. SUPPORTED needs a demonstrated trigger/incorrect effect and empty assumptions. NEEDS_CONTEXT requires an actionable visible concern plus a specific missing premise; unknown callers alone are not concerns. All evidence_lines are provided lines of the changed file, including line and a changed line. No changed HEAD lines means LIMITED.
Language failures do not require an application contract; ordinary valid operations do. Server observations are bounded examples, not full-program proof. Optional expression_repair must be the exact provided Python return expression and preserve established successful cases. Do not suggest a different return when the current return already satisfies the requirement.
